==Battleground==
*1 [[Swordsman (form 2) (Enemy)|Swordsman (form 2)]] spawns.
*1 [[Li'l Gau (form 2) (Enemy)|Li'l Gau (form 2)]] spawns after 4.67 seconds<sup>140f</sup>.
*1 [[Yurinchi (Enemy)|Yurinchi]] spawns after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Bridal Princess Punt (Enemy)|Bridal Princess Punt]] spawns as the boss.
**3 [[Dagshund]]s spawn, delay 36.67~40 seconds<sup>1,100f~1,200f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Croco]]s spawn, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
**1 [[Croco]] spawns.
**1 [[Squire Rel]] spawns.
**1 [[Croco]] spawns.
**1 [[Squire Rel]] spawns.
**1 [[Croco]] spawns.
**3 [[Duche]]s spawn, delay 36.67~40 seconds<sup>1,100f~1,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
*The [[Swordsman (form 2) (Enemy)|Swordsman]] does an insane 20,000 damage, but only has a meager 2,000 health and gives a lot of money when killed.
*[[Yurinchi (Enemy)|Yurinchi]] and [[Li'l Gau (form 2) (Enemy)|Li'l Gau]] are just something spawned to make the level feel like a collaboration stage; their attack power can barely hurt anything.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] can one-shot almost everything in this stage, including the Princess. Spawning him after the boss shockwave is your easiest way to win this stage.
*Using [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Giraffe Cat]] and [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Cats in a Box]] to slowly drain her health also works but takes more time.

